      "job_description_reference": "job_descriptions\\app_14a66f897623_role.txt",
      "job_description_text": "Rex.zone is hiring for entry-level STEM jobs in India supporting real AI/ML engineering workflows, including training data quality, RLHF evaluation, prompt evaluation, and QA evaluation for large language models. This is a remote, full-time role with structured workflows and calibration sessions.\n\nAbout The Role\n\nYou will support AI/ML teams by executing and improving data labeling and evaluation workflows used in LLM training pipelines across NLP, named entity recognition, computer vision annotation, and content safety labeling. You will follow annotation guidelines compliance, document edge cases, and help reduce ambiguity so models learn consistently.\n\nWhat You Will Do\n\nPerform data labeling for text and/or vision datasets to meet training data quality targets\nComplete RLHF-style preference ranking and response quality scoring to support model performance improvement\nRun prompt evaluation and QA evaluation to identify errors, hallucinations, policy violations, and formatting issues\nApply named entity recognition and taxonomy tagging using clear annotation guidelines compliance\nConduct content safety labeling for sensitive, policy, and restricted content categories\nAudit datasets for consistency, duplicates, label noise, and distribution gaps; propose fixes\nWrite concise rationales and escalate ambiguous cases to improve guidelines\nTrack throughput and quality metrics (accuracy, agreement rates) and participate in calibration sessions\nCollaborate with engineers and QA to validate changes to labeling rubrics and evaluation checklists\nSupport experimentation by comparing model outputs across variants and documenting findings\n\nRequired Skills\n\nSTEM fundamentals and strong analytical reasoning\nComfort with Python and SQL for basic data checks (filters, counts, joins) and simple scripts\nUnderstanding of NLP and/or computer vision annotation concepts\nExperience applying annotation guidelines compliance and documenting decisions\nAbility to perform QA evaluation, spot inconsistencies, and propose improvements\nClear written communication for rationales and issue reporting\n\nWorking Model\n\nRemote, distributed work with QA calibration and clear workflows.\n\nHigh accuracy and consistency are essential to improve training data quality.",
